2026-10-02T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2295) 'An unverified claim carries its confidence as a word and a probability.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2295) 'Agent replies stated forecasts and diagnoses in the same voice as checked facts. A reader cannot weigh a claim that does not say how sure it is.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2295) 'Run `scripts/check_confidence_tags.py` to check that each tag's number fits its word.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2295) 'agent replies state calibrated confidence
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2295) 'A claim an agent has not verified carries its confidence as a word and a probability in one tag: `(likely, p=0.80)`. The word comes from a fixed scale of five, and the number must fall inside that word's band. A verified fact (a command's output, a merged pull request, a passing gate) carries no tag. `scripts/check_confidence_tags.py` reads the bands from this RFD's source and fails any tag whose word and number disagree, so the scale and the gate cannot drift apart.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2295) 'The scale
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2295) 'The gate reads this table. A tag's number must lie inside its word's band, lower bound inclusive and upper bound exclusive, except that `almost certain` includes 1.00.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2295) '| word | lower | upper |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2295) '| --- | --- | --- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2295) '| remote | 0.00 | 0.10 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2295) '| unlikely | 0.10 | 0.40 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2295) '| even | 0.40 | 0.60 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2295) '| likely | 0.60 | 0.90 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2295) '| almost certain | 0.90 | 1.00 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2295) 'The tag
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2295) 'The form is `(word, p=0.NN)`: the word, a comma, `p=` and the probability with two decimals. It follows the claim it qualifies:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2295) '    The walker stays bit-deterministic (likely, p=0.75).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2295) '    The 12 modules finish today (unlikely, p=0.25).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2295) 'Only unverified claims carry a tag. A claim the agent checked in the same turn states the check instead of a probability, because a probability on a checked fact would hide that it was checked.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2295) 'Calibration
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2295) 'The numbers mean something only if they are calibrated: of the claims tagged `p=0.80`, about four in five should turn out true. A logbook entry that records tagged forecasts also records how they resolved, so the tags can be scored. No such score exists yet; the first logbook entry to carry tagged forecasts starts it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2295) 'Times
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2295) 'A time in a reply, a logbook entry, an issue comment or a pull request is written in ISO 8601 with its date and UTC offset: `2026-10-02T09:51-07:00`, not `09:51` or `11am`. A forecast's deadline is the same kind of time, so `tagged by 2026-10-02T11:00-07:00` is scorable by a reader in another zone or on another day.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2295) 'A piece of work is timed as an ISO 8601 interval, start and end, followed by its duration (operator, 2026-10-02): `2026-10-02T20:12:48+00:00/2026-10-02T20:40:10+00:00, PT27M22S`. Work still running gives its start and `open`. No gate checks this yet; it holds by agreement.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2295) 'Known unknowns
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2295) 'A plan or a recommendation ends with zero to four questions about the known unknowns whose answers would change it, each answerable in one word with the recommended option marked. None are asked when nothing is unknown, and never more than four (operator, 2026-10-02). Replies are not files, so this holds by agreement.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2295) 'Related
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2295) 'Lin, Hilton and Evans, "Teaching Models to Express Their Uncertainty in Words" (2022, DOI 10.48550/arXiv.2205.14334, registered with DataCite) is the method: a model states its confidence in words and numbers, and the statement is scored for calibration. RFD66606-2294 (agent knowledge lives in RFDs) is why the rule is here and not in a desk's memory. `CLAUDE.md`'s "How Work Is Verified" rule 3 (a silent skip reads like a pass) is why a verified fact and a guess must look different.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2295) 'What is checked
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2295) '`scripts/check_confidence_tags.py` scans `logbook/*.md` and every RFD source for tags, and fails a tag whose word is not on the scale or whose number falls outside the word's band. Its self-test plants one tag of each kind, a correct one, an unknown word and a number outside its band, and asserts the gate passes the first and fails the other two. Replies are not files, so the gate cannot see them; the rule holds there by agreement.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2295) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-02T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2295) 'On 2026-10-02 a reply described a Metal shader port as "Slang-to-MSL" when the shaders were hand-written, and the operator caught it. A bare percentage reads as code rather than as language.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2295  1 LINE
 Text:Written
